{
  "case_id": "2008-07-1090",
  "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1090",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Acting with express statutory authority and in furtherance of important foreign policies following the fall of the Saddam Hussein regime, the President made inapplicable with respect to Iraq all provisions of law that had applied to countries that sponsored terrorism."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1090",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under the plain language of the statute, those provisions included former section 1605(a)(7), which was a provision of law that applied only to such countries. Because section 1605(a)(7) was made inapplicable as to Iraq effective on the President's determination, it cannot now serve as the applicable statutory basis for abrogation of Iraq's foreign sovereign immunity and therefore subject matter jurisdiction in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1090",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Franklin, even if you are right about that, the legislation was an emergency measure with a sunset. It was revived for 1 year, but then no more. So, didn't this suspension of Iraq's lack of immunity -- didn't the immunity come back? Didn't the bar to immunity come back again once the emergency law sunsetted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1090",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, what do you make of the fact that in -- in 2008 Congress said that that was never its intention, it was never its intention for the President to have the authority to -- to do this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1090",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "EWSAA section 1503 authorized the President to make inapplicable with respect to Iraq any provision of law that applies to countries that have sponsored terrorism. The terrorism exception to the Foreign Sovereign Immunities Act falls squarely within the plain language of that authority. But if there were any question about that, certainly the President's exercise of his authority under that statute would be entitled to deference."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1090",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Wouldn't any such settlement have to take into account that Iraqi -- the Iraqi people themselves were the most numerous and probably the worst victims of the terror?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiffs",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1090",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But this does not mean -- and I think Justice Scalia's question was critical here. It does not mean that the plaintiffs are left without any remedy, rather that these plaintiffs have been put on the same footing as any other claimant against a foreign state that is not on the very small list of designated state sponsors of terrorism."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1090",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you saying it means any other provision of the law, except those that affect the jurisdiction of courts? Or are you saying any other provisions of law that relate to foreign assistance?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1090",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I actually do disagree and believe you can logically look at the statute -- in the sense that the word \"any\" means \"every,\" that is true."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1090",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right, is there any one other than that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1090",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, Justice Breyer, in -- the same point was made in cases like Atascadero and Raygor. \"Any\" means \"every\" except for the States. In that example."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1090",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, Mr. Goldstein, before you finish your argument, I'd like to know what you think about the claim for relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1090",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Solicitor General has it right. Post-Acree, these claims -- these types of claims were pleaded principally as State-law claims, and that has been recognized as providing a substantive cause of action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1090",
      "confidence": 0.0,
